00:01:31.476 --> 00:01:32.404
This is legit.

00:01:32.404 --> 00:01:33.565
- Lookin' good, lookin' good.

00:01:33.565 --> 00:01:34.680
- Thanks, brother.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.340
Isaac, why don't you
tell the Vayner Nation

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:38.102
a little bit about yourself, a
little bit about this project

00:01:38.102 --> 00:01:39.635
and I'm gonna push you off, not over.

00:01:39.635 --> 00:01:40.819
- No problem.

00:01:40.819 --> 00:01:42.038
- And I'll continue the show.

00:01:42.038 --> 00:01:43.141
- You got it, you got it.

00:01:43.141 --> 00:01:47.784
Basically, 9/11, Century 21 was destroyed,

00:01:47.784 --> 00:01:51.603
the Tower fell on this building

00:01:51.603 --> 00:01:53.635
and this whole building
was completely destroyed.

00:01:53.635 --> 00:01:55.400
We were closed for nine months,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.943
we almost went out of business

00:01:56.943 --> 00:01:59.776
and we decided that we
would stick it out here

00:01:59.776 --> 00:02:02.133
because we were here for 53 years

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:04.153
and we don't want the
terrorists to beat us

00:02:04.153 --> 00:02:06.939
so we stuck it out, we
were the only store open.

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:08.680
And then for many, many years

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.433
it was a thin line for
going out of business

00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:13.394
and finally this area
became better than ever,

00:02:13.394 --> 00:02:16.342
it's much better than it was before 2001.

00:02:16.342 --> 00:02:19.256
So Mr. Brainwash approached us and said,

00:02:19.256 --> 00:02:19.941
"Listen--"

00:02:19.941 --> 00:02:21.276
- Give a little context to Mr. Brainwash

00:02:21.276 --> 00:02:23.354
for, a quick little bio
for people that don't know.

00:02:23.354 --> 00:02:25.618
- Mr. Brainwash is a
very famous street artist

00:02:25.618 --> 00:02:29.112
and he lives in L.A. and
he's moving to New York

00:02:29.112 --> 00:02:32.119
and he also did Exit Through the Gift Shop

00:02:32.119 --> 00:02:35.613
which is a Academy Award
documentary about Banksy

00:02:35.613 --> 00:02:38.016
and he approached us and he said,

00:02:38.016 --> 00:02:39.769
"Listen, I want to get back to New York,

00:02:39.769 --> 00:02:41.290
"I'm moving from New York from L.A.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.192
"I want to make the people proud and happy

00:02:44.192 --> 00:02:46.096
"and change the whole vibe of the city.

00:02:46.096 --> 00:02:49.509
"I want to do a positive
tribute for New York City

00:02:49.509 --> 00:02:51.309
"representing 9/11."

00:02:51.309 --> 00:02:52.609
And we said, "Of course,

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:54.559
"we will lend you our
building to do this."

00:02:54.559 --> 00:02:57.775
Because we also are very civic minded

00:02:57.775 --> 00:02:59.318
and to tell you the truth

00:02:59.318 --> 00:03:01.455
when they did the mural
people were crying,

00:03:01.455 --> 00:03:04.369
people were writing on the
memorials on the bottom,

00:03:04.369 --> 00:03:06.901
1,000's of people came
hugging me, kissing me,

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.654
"Thank you for doing this for us."

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.059
- Did they kiss you on the lips?

00:03:10.059 --> 00:03:12.334
- Uh, the cute ones, ha ha.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:13.379
(laughing)

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:15.480
So that's the story, basically.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.920
- Why don't you tell, you know,

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.020
so obviously you can imagine
this means a lot to me,

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.437
but you'll see the
connection point in a minute.

00:03:20.437 --> 00:03:22.314
Why don't you tell for 5 seconds,

00:03:22.314 --> 00:03:23.683
this is a very
entrepreneurial business show,

00:03:23.683 --> 00:03:25.193
little story of your family's history

00:03:25.193 --> 00:03:28.257
as one of the great iconic
retailers in the region

00:03:28.257 --> 00:03:29.813
that I also grew up in.

00:03:29.813 --> 00:03:34.094
- Great question, we were 54 years old,

00:03:35.444 --> 00:03:40.444
my father and father's brother
established the company

00:03:41.145 --> 00:03:42.491
and basically, what they had was

00:03:42.491 --> 00:03:45.230
they had small ma and pa
stores all around the city

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.970
and then one day they
decided, sell 'em all

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.716
and open up a discount department store.

00:03:50.716 --> 00:03:52.678
So how did the name Century 21 come?

00:03:52.678 --> 00:03:54.756
There was a World's Fair in Chicago

00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:56.160
and they had like an Epcot Center

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.817
and Epcot Center was like
the city of the future

00:03:59.817 --> 00:04:01.837
and it was called Century 21 City.

00:04:01.837 --> 00:04:05.215
So my father said, "Let's make
this the store of the future,

00:04:05.215 --> 00:04:06.364
"Century 21."

00:04:06.364 --> 00:04:08.303
By the way we got it
before the real estate,

00:04:08.303 --> 00:04:10.300
so they can't sue us.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.380
- Whew.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.643
- Thank god, so that's how it started.

00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:16.023
- And you know one thing
that I just want to give you

00:04:16.023 --> 00:04:18.055
one last shout at that I think
everybody would love is,

00:04:18.055 --> 00:04:19.959
you know you're not a
14-year-old teenage girl,

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.735
but you were just
Snapchatting in the corner.

00:04:21.735 --> 00:04:23.534
Talk to me about your
personal relationship

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:24.997
with all this new innovation.

00:04:24.997 --> 00:04:26.842
What's your gut feel?

00:04:26.842 --> 00:04:27.772
Right in here.

00:04:27.772 --> 00:04:29.362
- I'm gonna tell you what it is.

00:04:29.362 --> 00:04:32.740
All our competitors, Loehmann's,
Daffy’s, Filene’s, Syms

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.331
all went out of business.

00:04:34.331 --> 00:04:36.896
They all started 54 years ago.

00:04:36.896 --> 00:04:40.275
The problem was they never
changed with the times.

00:04:40.275 --> 00:04:42.411
We're still here, we want to be relevant,

00:04:42.411 --> 00:04:45.255
we know that social
media is the way to go,

00:04:45.255 --> 00:04:46.532
we want to hit the millennials,

00:04:46.532 --> 00:04:49.399
we want to cater to them
other wise if we don't do that

00:04:49.399 --> 00:04:53.311
we gonna, God forbid, go
the way of our competitors.

00:04:53.311 --> 00:04:54.716
So we want to stay one-step
ahead of the group.

00:04:54.716 --> 00:04:57.096
And that's one thing that
always made Century 21 great,

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:59.255
we adopted to change.

00:04:59.255 --> 00:05:01.031
- My friend, I love you.

00:05:01.031 --> 00:05:02.274
- Love you too, buddy, good luck.

00:05:02.274 --> 00:05:03.597
- Thank you so much,
thank you for doing this.

00:05:03.597 --> 00:05:05.873
Fun show for me, fun to
have guys like that on.

00:05:05.873 --> 00:05:08.415
Now Andy Kay, AKA Leo,

00:05:08.415 --> 00:05:12.989
let's get into the show!

