00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.671
- [Voiceover] John asks,

00:06:07.671 --> 00:06:10.005
"How can entrepreneurs avoid
being soft in business?"

00:06:10.845 --> 00:06:12.188
- John I would argue

00:06:12.188 --> 00:06:14.383
that entrepreneurs should
be soft at business,

00:06:14.383 --> 00:06:15.683
I lead with my heart.

00:06:15.683 --> 00:06:18.469
I made 13 decisions today
that were predicated

00:06:18.469 --> 00:06:21.847
not on the dollars, but
on what made me feel good,

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:23.822
what feels right and
what the lifetime value

00:06:23.822 --> 00:06:26.421
of that decision is, how
it's gonna impact others.

00:06:26.421 --> 00:06:30.403
So I think there's a
completely wrong point of view

00:06:30.403 --> 00:06:32.168
that you need to be raw, unemotional.

00:06:32.168 --> 00:06:35.069
Family businesses don't stay
in business for 54 years

00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:36.765
if they made just decisions

00:06:36.765 --> 00:06:39.040
on the black and white bottom-line.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.967
I'm sure, what are some of the longer,

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:42.569
tenured employees over here.

00:06:42.569 --> 00:06:43.579
Get over here, Isaac.

00:06:43.579 --> 00:06:47.422
- We have employees for 26, 27 years.

00:06:47.422 --> 00:06:49.569
- And you don't get there

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:51.903
by just making black and
white financial decisions.

00:06:51.903 --> 00:06:52.704
- No.

00:06:52.704 --> 00:06:54.840
- I assume that you made tons of decisions

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.699
that didn't make the financial
sense at that moment?

00:06:56.699 --> 00:06:59.239
- We use common sense, common sense

00:06:59.239 --> 00:07:03.930
and we have a culture where
people love to work here,

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:06.229
they're all involved,
everybody has an idea,

00:07:06.229 --> 00:07:07.818
we listen to everybody's idea

00:07:07.818 --> 00:07:10.054
and they make a difference.

00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:11.511
- All right, Isaac, you gonna keep talking

00:07:11.511 --> 00:07:13.171
I'm gonna lose the show,
they're gonna be the Isaac Show,

00:07:13.171 --> 00:07:14.773
I'm gonna be out of
business, get out of here.

00:07:14.773 --> 00:07:15.748
- [Isaac] You called me.

00:07:15.748 --> 00:07:16.794
- I'm sorry but I messed up.

00:07:16.794 --> 00:07:18.130
The bottom line is that's it guys,

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.569
you're not in business for 54 years,

00:07:19.569 --> 00:07:20.869
two generations, three generations.

00:07:20.869 --> 00:07:25.525
You gotta make calls that don't
just lead with your wallet,

00:07:25.525 --> 00:07:26.790
it needs to come with your heart.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.090
I actually think the future

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:29.890
of entrepreneurship
businesses that are big

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.513
will actually be considered
soft by today's standards.

00:07:32.513 --> 00:07:34.034
Because if you're gonna go too hard,

00:07:34.034 --> 00:07:36.727
there's too many alternatives
for people to do other things

00:07:36.727 --> 00:07:38.190
than to work in that environment

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.850
as all these opportunities arise.

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:43.263
So I'm a proud, soft entrepreneur.

00:07:43.263 --> 00:07:45.550
- [Voiceover] MAngiolillo
says, "Waiting for

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:48.591
"Jab, Jab, Jab, Right Hook to
ship from Amazon, and asks,

00:07:48.591 --> 00:07:51.295
"Does your theory still
work in the Italian Market?"

00:07:51.955 --> 00:07:53.563
- MAngiolillo, thank you so much,

00:07:53.563 --> 00:07:55.442
does it work in the Italian market?

00:07:55.442 --> 00:07:58.568
Does giving, giving, giving and then ask

00:07:58.568 --> 00:08:00.240
work in the Italian Market?

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.505
Does provide value, provide
value, provide value

00:08:02.505 --> 00:08:04.245
and then build equity and leverage

00:08:04.245 --> 00:08:05.744
to get something in return,

00:08:05.744 --> 00:08:07.357
does that work in the Italian market?

00:08:07.357 --> 00:08:08.924
It works in the human market,

00:08:08.924 --> 00:08:10.899
obviously every market
is a little bit different

00:08:10.899 --> 00:08:12.500
and there's suppressed governments

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.366
and there's dynamics, communism
creates different behaviors.

00:08:15.366 --> 00:08:17.317
You know there's a million
different variables,

00:08:17.317 --> 00:08:21.543
but at the end of day
humans absolutely respond

00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:25.362
to being guilted or feel
compelled to return favors

00:08:25.362 --> 00:08:27.599
or do good for people
that give good to them.

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:29.061
So when you're providing value upfront,

00:08:29.061 --> 00:08:32.231
whether you're in Italy or
in Egypt or the Soviet Union,

00:08:32.231 --> 00:08:36.259
Syria, Afghanistan, Argentina, New Zealand

00:08:36.259 --> 00:08:38.859
it's going to work, it's
not gonna work on everybody.

00:08:38.859 --> 00:08:41.251
Do I believe there's cultures, countries

00:08:41.251 --> 00:08:43.953
that there's more upside
within based on the DNA

00:08:43.953 --> 00:08:46.147
and the overall stereotypes of a country?

00:08:46.147 --> 00:08:48.771
I do, I absolutely do, but in general

00:08:48.771 --> 00:08:50.548
this is an absolute winning formula

00:08:50.548 --> 00:08:53.588
not to mention that it's
a winning formula for you

00:08:53.588 --> 00:08:55.005
not just your results.

00:08:55.005 --> 00:08:57.802
You need to feel good about
providing upfront value.

00:08:57.802 --> 00:08:59.683
You know, I'm not gonna go,

00:08:59.683 --> 00:09:02.388
I'm not gonna judge my life
on how much money I made,

00:09:02.388 --> 00:09:03.571
I'm gonna judge my life

00:09:03.571 --> 00:09:05.421
by how many people
showed up to my funeral.

00:09:05.421 --> 00:09:07.103
So the process works for me,

00:09:07.103 --> 00:09:08.857
not just on the financial aspect,

00:09:08.857 --> 00:09:10.714
but on who I wanna be as a human being

00:09:10.714 --> 00:09:13.221
and you need to ask that question for you.

00:09:13.221 --> 00:09:14.604
- [Voiceover] Ayoub says, "Hi Gary,

00:09:14.604 --> 00:09:16.356
"you told me in a previous
video that students

00:09:16.356 --> 00:09:18.457
