00:09:21.336 --> 00:09:23.078
- I believe that if you go to college

00:09:23.078 --> 00:09:26.038
and collect debt to be an
entrepreneur, not a doctor,

00:09:26.038 --> 00:09:29.115
not a lawyer, not a
consultant at Baynor McKinsey

00:09:29.115 --> 00:09:30.542
where you have to go to
an Ivy League school,

00:09:30.542 --> 00:09:31.796
graduate and leverage that.

00:09:31.796 --> 00:09:35.418
But a true entrepreneur,
like father and brother,

00:09:35.418 --> 00:09:37.357
go out there and hustle, be a merchant.

00:09:37.357 --> 00:09:40.816
You know, that to me
is a crazy proposition

00:09:40.816 --> 00:09:42.999
to collect debt for in a 2016 world.

00:09:42.999 --> 00:09:45.112
So what I think they should
do instead is go work.

00:09:45.112 --> 00:09:47.398
Literally just go work,
I mean think about it,

00:09:47.398 --> 00:09:51.600
instead of going $80,000 in
debt, you can go work for $1

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.654
and be way up in the pot,
you can work for free

00:09:54.654 --> 00:09:56.175
and be on the way positive.

00:09:56.175 --> 00:09:58.857
And speaking of that, that
speaks to my next strategy.

00:09:58.857 --> 00:10:03.373
Go work for somebody,
a woman that you admire

00:10:03.373 --> 00:10:06.239
the way she did it and
take a lot less money

00:10:06.239 --> 00:10:08.933
working in her organization
than somebody else

00:10:08.933 --> 00:10:11.928
because you're trying to
sap the IP out of her,

00:10:11.928 --> 00:10:13.356
out of that leadership.

00:10:13.356 --> 00:10:14.749
So not only go work,

00:10:14.749 --> 00:10:17.697
go work for the lowest
possible way you can survive.

00:10:17.697 --> 00:10:19.416
Go live with four roommates
in a studio apartment

00:10:19.416 --> 00:10:21.529
and eat fast food if you have too.

00:10:21.529 --> 00:10:23.757
You can go lose that weight
later, like the I did.

00:10:23.757 --> 00:10:25.719
The bottom line is you need to go work

00:10:25.719 --> 00:10:27.437
in an environment that inspires you

00:10:27.437 --> 00:10:30.141
and really you want it to be a place

00:10:30.141 --> 00:10:32.035
that you want to be like.

00:10:32.035 --> 00:10:33.799
To go work for somebody
that you want to be like

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:36.457
is a tremendous value
proposition for an entrepreneur.

00:10:36.457 --> 00:10:38.500
When I think about what Andy and DRock

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.578
have been affected by through osmosis,

00:10:40.578 --> 00:10:42.993
they're probably scared to think about

00:10:42.993 --> 00:10:44.572
some of the tendencies they now have

00:10:44.572 --> 00:10:46.801
that are my tendencies
because I've affected it.

00:10:46.801 --> 00:10:49.621
It's crazy how it works, it's crazy,

00:10:49.621 --> 00:10:51.699
you should see the ego all 600 people

00:10:51.699 --> 00:10:54.312
at VaynerMedia walk around
with, it's disgusting.

00:10:54.312 --> 00:10:56.819
But the bottom line is
it's affected from the top

00:10:56.819 --> 00:10:59.478
so go work for somebody you
admire and want to replicate

00:10:59.478 --> 00:11:03.854
and regardless of the cost,
if you're a true entrepreneur.

00:11:03.854 --> 00:11:05.631
- [Voiceover] Elite Sports Tipster asks,

00:11:05.631 --> 00:11:08.439
"If you were starting again
and needed to make $2K/m

00:11:08.439 --> 00:11:10.931
"in as few hours as
possible, what would you do?"

00:11:11.899 --> 00:11:15.412
- If I was starting again
and I had to make $2,000

00:11:15.412 --> 00:11:18.952
as quickly as possible, what would I do?

00:11:18.952 --> 00:11:21.134
Without all the brand equity
I have, obviously right?

00:11:22.364 --> 00:11:24.422
It's funny usually I
say go to a garage sale,

00:11:24.422 --> 00:11:27.963
I'd probably go to Century 21, buy stuff

00:11:27.963 --> 00:11:29.808
and flip it on Ebay on the arbitrage

00:11:29.808 --> 00:11:31.144
cause they're such a discounter

00:11:31.144 --> 00:11:33.770
or Wine Library and return
the wine to another store

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:34.989
that charges more for it.

00:11:34.989 --> 00:11:37.381
Deep down, the joke is
and I'm making a fun joke,

00:11:37.381 --> 00:11:40.027
garage saling, Goodwill, I'm a merchant.

00:11:40.027 --> 00:11:42.848
Buying something for less
than what I can sell it for

00:11:42.848 --> 00:11:44.126
is what I'm really good at.

00:11:44.126 --> 00:11:45.984
With no money, with not a lot of money

00:11:45.984 --> 00:11:48.723
and I have to make 2K, the
quickest arbitrage I know

00:11:48.723 --> 00:11:50.546
in today's society, is to go to places,

00:11:50.546 --> 00:11:53.586
buy it and flip it on Ebay,
the speed is very quickly.

00:11:53.586 --> 00:11:56.268
That is literally what I
would do, I know my strengths.

00:11:56.268 --> 00:11:58.104
If I was to have to build up again,

00:11:58.104 --> 00:12:01.446
you know, imagine I did fail
and made some critical mistakes

00:12:01.446 --> 00:12:02.805
and lost everything.

00:12:02.805 --> 00:12:04.709
First I would have to
rectify my family situation,

00:12:04.709 --> 00:12:06.519
but then I make a lot of money

00:12:06.519 --> 00:12:08.238
and I've had a lot of
success at being right

00:12:08.238 --> 00:12:10.686
for the last 20 years,
that's what I live off of.

00:12:10.686 --> 00:12:12.997
If I was then to be so crazy wrong

00:12:12.997 --> 00:12:14.878
that I went out of business,

00:12:14.878 --> 00:12:16.445
I would no longer be able to rely

00:12:16.445 --> 00:12:18.257
on my advice as my foundation,

00:12:18.257 --> 00:12:20.677
so I'd have to go back
to the way I built it

00:12:20.677 --> 00:12:23.759
in the first place which is
truly sales, selling stuff.

00:12:23.759 --> 00:12:26.005
Deep down I'm a salesman,
you know the truth is,

00:12:26.005 --> 00:12:27.261
I need to spend more time

00:12:27.261 --> 00:12:28.467
and I encourage you Vayner Nation

00:12:28.467 --> 00:12:30.057
to ask me more sales questions

00:12:30.057 --> 00:12:31.358
because I think I have a lot more

00:12:31.358 --> 00:12:32.983
to offer publicly around sales.

00:12:32.983 --> 00:12:34.922
This show has allowed me to talk

00:12:34.922 --> 00:12:37.162
a lot more about HR,
management, leadership.

00:12:37.162 --> 00:12:38.776
The one category where I think

00:12:38.776 --> 00:12:41.085
I've disproportionately
under-serviced my community,

00:12:41.085 --> 00:12:43.163
is a lot more about my sales skills

00:12:43.163 --> 00:12:44.836
which are really the
disproportional skills

00:12:44.836 --> 00:12:47.865
that grew Wine Library while
the technology was catching up.

00:12:47.865 --> 00:12:49.282
The first year of Wine Library

00:12:49.282 --> 00:12:50.977
went from three to nine million

00:12:50.977 --> 00:12:53.484
just because I was on the floor.

00:12:53.484 --> 00:12:57.688
So yeah, I would say that, sales.

00:12:57.688 --> 00:12:58.807
That's it, that's a wrap.

